# Feature inventory

When you implement, materially change, or remove a **user-facing or product capability**, update [`FEATURES.md`](../../FEATURES.md) in the **same change**.

Do this for:

- New MCP tools or tool arguments
- Trip-logic behavior (geocode, continuity, later fact-checking, routing, …)
- Widget / map UI behavior
- Integration or validation paths that change how the product is proven

Skip for:

- Pure refactors with no behavior change
- Test-only or comment-only edits
- Dependency bumps that do not change product behavior

Each feature entry must include: **name**, **expected behavior**, **category**, **status**, **where it lives**, **out of scope**, **how to verify**.

Use an existing category when it fits (`trip logic`, `fact checking`, `MCP tool`, `UI`, `integration`, `validation`). Add a short new category only when none fit.

Set **status** honestly (`shipped`, `local only`, `planned`). After commit/push of previously local work, flip status to `shipped`.

**Future development:** ideas not yet built go under the **Future development** section with status `planned`. When one of those ships, move it into the main feature list (status `shipped`) and fill in real **where it lives** / **how to verify**. When a design discussion agrees on later work (e.g. ops logging, routing), add a planned entry there in the same change if it is not already listed.

Before finishing a feature task, confirm `FEATURES.md` reflects the new behavior — including **out of scope** so later work (e.g. rider fact-checking vs wrong-place hold) stays distinct.
